BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Oldest Person in the World
DTSTART:20261202T033000Z
DTEND:20261202T051000Z
DTSTAMP:20261202T033000Z
UID:oi8v8qgZK8
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 82 mins (1h22m)\n\nA decade-long global journey chro
 nicles the ever-changing record holders of the title of oldest person aliv
 e. What begins as a portrait of longevity becomes a meditation on the pass
 age of time\, the randomness of fate\, and the joy and profound human expe
 rience of being alive. Virtual Q&A with Director Sam Green\n\nhttps://www
 .siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/the-oldest-person-in-the-world\n\nEstimated s
 tart: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Twilight (2008)
DTSTART:20261207T000000Z
DTEND:20261207T022500Z
DTSTAMP:20261207T000000Z
UID:QUYCxEONDN
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 127 mins (2h07m)\n\nSIFF Book ClubIt's time to get c
 ozy this winter with Twilight! We're reading (or rereading for the umptee
 nth time) Stephenie Meyer's bestselling novel and then watching (or rewatc
 hing for the zillionth time) Catherine Hardwicke's adaptation\, presented 
 in 35mm. Arrive early to check out Beguiled Books’ swoon-worthy selectio
 ns and local artist Chloe Ladwig’s Cullen-approved prints. Forever Twili
 ght in Forks will be joining us too! Chat with them in the lobby to learn 
 more about their festival and collection.  In recognition of the flawed w
 ay in which the “Twilight” book and film series depict the Quileute Tr
 ibe\, we're donating a portion of ticket proceeds to the Quileute Move to 
 Higher Ground Project\, and we encourage you to do the same to the extent 
 that you are able.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/siff-book-c
 lub/twilight\n\nEstimated start: 16:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Damnation (1988)
DTSTART:20261208T023000Z
DTEND:20261208T044500Z
DTSTAMP:20261208T023000Z
UID:BD8AgxDk8B
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club4K restoration. A
  mid-career masterwork by legendary Hungarian art house auteur Béla Tarr 
 and the first of his internationally acclaimed trilogy of films written in
  collaboration with author László Krasznahorkai (including the legendary
  Sátántangó).Intro by Cinema Worker Adam Plesser.\n\nhttps://www.siff.n
 et/programs-and-events/siff-movie-club/damnation\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mountains on Stage - Winter Edition 2026
DTSTART:20261210T030000Z
DTEND:20261210T063000Z
DTSTAMP:20261210T030000Z
UID:MHcAUn82b8
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 195 mins (3h15m)\n\nMountains on Stage is an interna
 tional mountain film festival showcasing a selection of inspiring adventur
 e\, climbing\, skiing\, mountaineering\, and outdoor films. Each screening
  features several short and medium-length documentaries celebrating explor
 ation\, human achievement\, and the natural world.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net
 /cinema/in-theaters/mountains-on-stage-winter-edition-2026\n\nEstimated st
 art: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Muppet Christmas Carol (1992)
DTSTART:20261212T220000Z
DTEND:20261212T234500Z
DTSTAMP:20261212T220000Z
UID:982nr58LD2
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 89 mins (1h29m)\n\nSIFF Holiday Favorites Charles Di
 ckens’ timeless tale of Ebenezer Scrooge (Michael Caine)\, his cold hear
 t\, and how the Ghosts of Christmas Past\, Present\, and Future seek to sh
 ow him the error of his ways comes to life through the magic of Jim Henson
 ’s Muppets. Recently remastered\, including the original song "When Love
  is Gone." Arrive 30 minutes early for an exciting Muppet pre-show special
 ! All ages welcome ($5 tickets for children aged 2-12 years old\, free for
  under 2).\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/holiday-favorites/t
 he-muppet-christmas-carol\n\nEstimated start: 14:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
